#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "faed85bb-89ce-5a06-b08b-d84b4c3cd7a9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164004} {:answer-field/id #uuid "18a50378-7dea-5125-b1f1-8186b60315c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164005}] :question/id #uuid "17eee175-34bb-5ca1-9aad-a080088cd275" :question/math-academy-id "q-322280" :question/problem "${x_{1}^{′}(t) = x_{1}(t); x_{2}^{′}(t) =-x_{1}(t) + 3x_{2}(t),x(0) = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_{1}(s) = L{x_{1}(t)}$ and $X_{2}(s) = L{x_{2}(t)}$. In terms of the parameter $s$, the solution of the new system is$X_{1}(s) =$ {{field-1}},\n$X_{2}(s) =$ {{field-2}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303387} :answer-field/id #uuid "518f0276-0f4b-5c49-a892-c180fc62763c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303953} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcc71fe-ab2d-5096-8ba2-82ce4b706e91" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c4c84fb-7fb4-580a-bff4-417ed1ebd433" :question/math-academy-id "q-331918" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-2{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}+4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get \n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s)$ gives\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3(\\frac{3}{s+2})+4{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302842} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f9ccbb-98c5-5a7d-8a34-9b6a924b104f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3ce928a-a5a9-5225-8c9f-2f61190156c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3ce928a-a5a9-5225-8c9f-2f61190156c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b95b873-f263-55a4-aa11-176bdc917560" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304494} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b600c94-694f-5df9-8995-92f0759d4e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b600c94-694f-5df9-8995-92f0759d4e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303219} :answer-field/id #uuid "a99db976-4eb3-54c9-b026-70c5ab583549" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c87bd0e-68f0-53c0-a1da-53a949f4133b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c87bd0e-68f0-53c0-a1da-53a949f4133b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303021} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee8a77b9-f4f3-5da7-a356-159e03040e12" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "317fc248-dee8-522d-9f3a-ce7380dbab1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332439" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ 5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
